        "original_id": "cd2f78ef-a0cf-5092-aee7-e2e2c851d589",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Severin\n- Organizations: EC Comics, Marvel Comics\n- Products: Two-Fisted Tales, Frontline Combat, Cracked, Mad\n- Topics: comics, war comics, Western comics, satiric magazines\n\nFacts:\n- John Powers Severin was born on December 26, 1921, and he died on February 12, 2012.\n- Cracked was founded in 1958.\n- Cracked was launched in the wake of Mad magazine and proved to be the most durable of the many similar publications.\n- John Severin was an American comics artist known for distinctive work with EC Comics on the war comics Two-Fisted Tales and Frontline Combat.\n- John Severin was also known for work for Marvel Comics, especially its war and Western comics.\n- John Severin had a 45-year stint with the satiric magazine Cracked.",
